@startuml workflow
' The whole process, from installing meerkat to the complaint.
' Render: docs/manual/render.sh (needs plantuml); commit the SVG too.
skinparam defaultFontName sans-serif
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FCFCFB
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #52514E
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FCFCFB
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #52514E
skinparam ArrowColor #52514E
skinparam SwimlaneBorderColor #C3C2B7
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FDF3DC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #FAB219
title meerkat: from installation to complaint

|#E8F0FB|You|
start
:Install meerkat and the Ookla CLI;
:Put the contract figures in the config
(**[contract]**, from the product information sheet);
:Connect the computer by **cable**;
:**sudo meerkat check**;
:**sudo systemctl enable --now meerkat**;

|#FCFCFB|meerkat (service)|
repeat
  :Connectivity probe (every 30 s)
  and speed test (every 30 min);
  :Append to speed.csv, connectivity.csv, raw/;
  if (just after midnight UTC?) then (yes)
    :Seal the day:
    SHA-256 manifest;
  endif
repeat while (2–4 weeks of data?) is (not yet)
->enough;

|You|
:**meerkat advise-bbm**
the slowest days and hours;
:Enter the contract figures **by hand**
in the Breitbandmessung app;

repeat
  :Campaign day (3 days, one free day between,
  all within 14 days);
  |#FDF3DC|Breitbandmessung app|
  :5 measurements
  (5 min or more apart);
  note right
    While the app runs, meerkat
    holds its speed tests
    (paused_official).
  end note
  :3 hours or more later:
  5 more measurements;
  |You|
repeat while (3 days measured?) is (no)
->yes;

|Breitbandmessung app|
:Export the results: CSV and PDF protocol;

|You|
:**sudo meerkat import-bbm** the CSV and PDF;
:**meerkat verify**: the trail is intact;
:**meerkat report**: the official finding first,
meerkat's long-term data as support;
if (deviation in the official campaign?) then (yes)
  :**meerkat export**: one ZIP
  (report, data, protocol, checksums);
  :Complaint to the provider
  (reduction of payment, § 57 TKG);
else (no)
  :Keep recording; repeat the campaign
  when the line gets worse;
endif
stop
@enduml
